 "notes": [
  "The parts list matched the sensors to ntc-temperature-sensor, but the circuit image and schematic show force-sensitive resistors (FSRs), so the catalogue type fsr was used.",
  "The FSR legs are extended with red and blue hook-up wires in the image. Each is modelled as a jumper wire joined (clipped) to an FSR lead at one end and plugged into the breadboard at the other.",
  "Breadboard rail hole numbers (tp/tn/bp/bn) are approximated from the picture. Only the rail they belong to matters electrically.",
  "Sensor 1 (the left FSR, column 6) feeds A1 and sensor 2 (the right FSR, column 16) feeds A0, following the yellow wire routing in the image.",
  "Each FSR connects between the bottom + rail (5V) and its divider node. A 10K resistor runs from that node to the bottom - rail (GND).",
  "The pushbutton straddles the centre gap in columns 5 and 7. Column 5 (5V) is side 1 and column 7 (pin 2 and the 10K pull-down to GND) is side 2.",
  "The top and bottom rails are linked by a red wire (+) and a black wire (-) at the right-hand end of the breadboard.",
  "Resistor values are 10 k\u03a9, given as 10000 in the value prop."
 ],
